  "major": "media-screen-studies-ba-nyc-4014e9c0",
  "major_name": "Media and Screen Studies",
  "degree": "BA",
  "campus": "New York",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "The Bachelor of Arts in Media and Screen Studies offers courses in analysis and practice. Required courses offer students an opportunity to obtain the critical-thinking skills necessary to better understand media content, media technology, and media production. Students then decide how many production and analysis courses they want to take. Choosing from a broad range of electives, students can take more than half their major in media and film production courses, can take a majority of courses that critically examine media content and technology, or can combine courses in other ways. This program is currently only available to former Marymount Manhattan College students who are eligible for continued enrollment at Northeastern University. This program includes required courses that will be taught on ground at the Northeastern New York City campus.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nBA Language Requirements\nAll BA students are required to complete the BA degree language requirements, for a total of 12 semester hours of language study or demonstrated equivalent proficiency, as described in\nAdditional Requirements for BA students\n. Successful demonstration of proficiency does not reduce total minimum semester hours of study required to earn the BA degree.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nNUpath requirements Interpreting Culture (IC) and Societies and Institutions (SI) are met through the major course requirements.\nNUpath requirements Creative Expression/Innovation (EI), Differences and Diversity (DD), and Ethical Reasoning (ER) may be met through electives in the major.\nNUpath requirements Natural and Designed World (ND), Formal and Quantitative Reasoning (FQ), and Analyzing and Using Data (AD) must be met through general electives.\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences Requirements\nAll undergraduate students enrolled in programs at the New York campus are required to fulfill\nNew York State Liberal Arts and Sciences requirements\n.\nMedia and Screen Studies Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nCommon Requirements\nMSCR 1220\nMedia, Culture, and Society\n4\nMSCR 2220\nUnderstanding Media\n4\nCluster Courses\nCritical Analysis\nComplete 4 semester hours from the following:\n4\nMSCR 1420\nMedia History\nMSCR 2300\nTelevision: Text and Context\nMSCR 2895\nFilm Analysis\nMedia Production\nComplete 4 semester hours from the following:\n4\nMSCR 1230\nIntroduction to Film Production\nMSCR 2391\nIntroduction to Screenwriting\nMedia Cultures\nComplete 4 semester hours from the following:\n4\nMSCR 2325\nGlobal Media\nMSCR 2335\nRace and Social Justice in American Film\nMSCR 3392\nGender and Film\nMSCR 3437\nMedia and Identity\nWriting-Intensive Seminars\nComplete 8 semester hours from the following:\n8\nMSCR 2600\nCloud, Closet, (Drop)Box\nMSCR 3330\nDocumentary Film Ethics\nMSCR 3420\nDigital Media Culture\nMSCR 3422\nMedia Audiences\nMSCR 3600\nFilm Theory\nMSCR 3700\nQueer Media\nMedia and Screen Studies Electives\nComplete 20 semester hours from the following:\n20\nARTD 2360\nIntroduction to Photography\nARTD 3480\nVideo: Sound and Image\nARTD 3485\nExperimental Video\nMSCR courses between MSCR 1200-4999 that have not been used to satisfy other degree requirements\nCapstone Experience Course\nMSCR 4623\nMedia and Screen Studies Capstone\n4\nSupporting Courses\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nIntroduction to College\nMSCR 1000\nMedia and Screen Studies at Northeastern\n1\nWriting Requirements\nFirst-Year Writing\nENGW 1111\nFirst-Year Writing\n4\nor\nENGW 1102\nFirst-Year Writing for Multilingual Writers\nor\nENGW 1114\nFirst-Year Writing with Service-Learning\nAdvanced Writing Across the Disciplines\nENGW 3314\nAdvanced Writing in the Arts, Media, and Design\n4\nor\nENGW 3315\nInterdisciplinary Advanced Writing in the Disciplines\nMedia and Screen Studies Grade Requirement\nNo more than two grades below a C in media and screen studies courses may be used to satisfy degree requirements.\nOptional Co-op\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nSuccessful completion of EXED 2000 is required for participation in co-op.\nEXED 2000\nProfessional Development for Co-op\n1\nCOOP 3945\nCo-op Work Experience\n0\nor\nCOOP 3946\nCo-op Work Experience--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3947\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad--Half Time\nor\nCOOP 3948\nCo-op Work Experience Abroad\nMajor Credit Requirement\nComplete 52 semester hours in the major.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
